  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-12-03T00:05:06.592Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "**This is a tested Issue!**\nI have recently purchased and installed a brand new RTX 3070 and have been experiencing extremely low framerate issues.\nThese are the ways I've tried to solve this issue:\n*Updating Drivers\n*Testing All Older Drivers\n*Optimized Avatars\n*Off and On Compatibility Mode\n*Optimized Worlds\n*Reinstalling VRChat\n*Clearing Cache\n*Checking Drivers For Other Components\n*Changing GPU (GTX 1080)\n*Less RAM\n*More RAM\n*VRChat Settings (vrhigh,vrlow,desktoplow)\n*Different RAM\nHere are some Framerate Comparisons:\n32GB RAM\nVR w/3070 = 40-58fps\nDesktop w/3070 = 53-60fps\nVR w/1080 = 89-90fps\nDesktop w/1080 = 90-91 fps\n16GB RAM\nVR w/3070 = 37-54fps\nDesktop w/3070 = 53-60fps\nVR w/1080 = 80-89fps\nDesktop w/1080 = 88-90 fps\n*These results were achieved in the default Alien in a basic standard shader plane with no mirror and no customization further than the default VRCworld prefab*\nHere is My Spec List for Reference:\nCPU: Ryzen 2600\nRAM: 32GB Corsair LPX 3600Mhz\nGPU: Gigabyte AORUS Master RTX 3070\nMotherboard: Asus B450-F Gaming\nPSU: EVGA 80+ Gold 750w\nIf you need to reach out to me my discord is ミルク#6969\nThank you, and I hope the team can quickly fix this issue.",
